all_tasks.description:
Create the AI channel clusterer system prompt and define the structured diff response format.

System prompt (agents/clusterer.md or similar):
- Role: Categorize tasks into topic channels based on theme and code locality
- Input: New task (subject, description), current channel list with active tasks, recently completed tasks
- Output: Structured JSON diff with: create_channels, archive_channels, merge_channels, assign_tasks
- Constraints: Don't reassign in-flight tasks, archive channels when all tasks complete, merge when themes converge, main channel is separate (receives cross-posts only), consider code locality (tasks touching same files belong together)

Define the ClusteringDiff struct in Rust:
```rust
struct ClusteringDiff {
    create_channels: Vec<CreateChannel>,   // { name, tasks }
    archive_channels: Vec<String>,
    merge_channels: Vec<MergeChannel>,     // { from, into }
    assign_tasks: Vec<TaskAssignment>,     // { task, channel }
}
```

Add parsing/validation for the clusterer's JSON response. Use haiku model to keep costs low.

